## Intuition
Based on the formula that sum on n elements = n*n+1/2

## Approach
Get maximum and minimum value of array to find the range.
Now if all elements are consecutive then the array sum will always be (sum till maximum - sum till minimum-1)

## Solution
```java[]
class Solution {
    public boolean isConsecutive(int[] nums) {
        // Your code goes here
        int minimum = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
        int maximum = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        for(int i = 0;i<nums.length;i++){
            minimum = Math.min(minimum, nums[i]);
            maximum = Math.max(maximum, nums[i]);
        }
        // Sum till minimum -1
        long preSum = (long)(minimum-1)*(long)(minimum)/2;
        long totalSum = (long)(maximum)*(long)(maximum+1)/2;
        long expectedSum = totalSum-preSum;

        // Sum of array
        long sum = 0;
        for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++){
            sum+= (long)(nums[i]);
        }
        return sum==expectedSum;
    }
}
```

